    "auto_generated": true,
    "text": "A Bayesian ANOVA compared 5 models for len (fixed-effect prior scale r = 0.500).\n\nThe best model is 'supp + dose + supp:dose' with posterior probability 0.727 and BF₁₀ = 7.67 × 10¹⁴ against the null model (extreme evidence for H₁).\n\nModel-averaged inclusion Bayes factors: supp BF = 140; dose BF = 3.20 × 10¹⁴; dose:supp BF = 10.6."
  },
  "notes": [],
  "module": "bayes_anova",
  "module_version": "1.0.0",
  "title": "Bayesian ANOVA",
  "status": "ok",
  "code": "library(BayesFactor)\nlibrary(bayestestR)\nlibrary(ggnext)\n# Bayesian ANOVA: len by supp, dose\nd <- data[complete.cases(data[, c(\"len\", \"supp\", \"dose\")]), c(\"len\", \"supp\", \"dose\")]\nd$supp <- factor(d$supp)\nd$dose <- factor(d$dose)\ndesc <- aggregate(len ~ supp, data = d, FUN = function(x)\n  c(n = length(x), mean = mean(x), sd = sd(x), se = sd(x) / sqrt(length(x))))\nset.seed(123)\nbf <- anovaBF(len ~ supp * dose, data = d,\n  whichModels = \"withmain\", rscaleFixed = 0.5, progress = FALSE)\nx <- extractBF(bf)\nmodels <- data.frame(model = c(\"Null model\", rownames(x)), bf10 = c(1, x$bf), error = c(NA, x$error))\nmodels$p_post <- models$bf10 / sum(models$bf10)   # P(M|data), all models equally likely a priori\nmodels <- models[order(-models$bf10), ]\ninclusion <- bayesfactor_inclusion(bf)\nd_ci <- do.call(rbind, lapply(split(d$len, d$supp), function(v) {\n  v <- v[!is.na(v)]; m <- mean(v); h <- qt(0.975, length(v) - 1) * sd(v) / sqrt(length(v))\n  data.frame(mean = m, lower = m - h, upper = m + h)\n}))\nd_ci$supp <- factor(rownames(d_ci), levels = rownames(d_ci))\np <- ggnext(d_ci, aes(supp, mean, ymin = lower, ymax = upper)) +\n  geom_pointrange() +\n  labs(title = \"len by supp\", x = \"Supplement\", y = \"Tooth length\") +\n  theme_modern()",
